#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""sb: fast, channel-aware search over your second brain (read-only).

Usage:
    sb <query...> [--channel <one of second_brain.channels>] [--limit N]
                  [--raw] [--engine auto|rg|python] [--config PATH]
    sb --doctor [--config PATH]
    sb --init-key
    sb --hash-name < words.txt
    sb --help

The usage text names the configured channels, e.g.
`--channel dance-school|other-activities`, generated from the config.

Config: the `second_brain:` block of kit.config.yaml, read with a stdlib
subset parser (no PyYAML). The file is the first of: --config PATH,
$KIT_CONFIG, $KIT_HOME/kit.config.yaml, $HOME/grok-kit/kit.config.yaml. An
explicit --config or $KIT_CONFIG that does not exist is an error; otherwise
no file means built-in defaults, equal to kit.config.example.yaml. A key
left empty (`key:` with nothing below it) takes its default.
    home            SB_HOME; $SB_HOME wins over it. `${VAR}` is expanded from
                    the environment (`${KIT_HOME}` falls back to kit.home), a
                    leading `~` is $HOME, a relative path is relative to the
                    config file's folder; an unset variable is an error.
    router_file     relative to home (default ROUTER.md)
    channels        the channel names (default dance-school, other-activities);
                    non-empty, unique, no whitespace or any of , + | / [ ] " '
    roots           folders searched, relative to home (default ["."]);
                    missing ones are skipped
    raw_roots       searched only with --raw (default [])
    path_defaults   folder prefix -> channel, used when a note names no
                    channel (default "<channel>/" -> channel for every
                    configured channel); the longest matching prefix wins;
                    every value must be a configured channel
    name_hashes     first 16 hex chars of HMAC-SHA256(scan key, folded
                    word) -> channel; extra channel detection, default {}
                    (empty); entries need the scan key (below)
    boost_paths     path prefixes whose files get a fixed score bonus
                    (default [])
    doctor          fail_on_untagged (check 2), fail_on_multiple_channels (3),
                    fail_on_folder_mismatch (4), fail_on_cross_channel_link
                    (5), fail_on_missing_router_path (1); all true by default;
                    false turns that check's FAIL line into a WARN line
Parser subset: block mappings by space indentation, `- item` block lists of
scalars, one-line flow lists `[a, "b"]` and flow mappings `{}` /
`{"k": "v"}`, double- and single-quoted or plain scalars, true/false, integers,
`#` comments outside quotes. Tabs in indentation, unterminated quotes, bad
indentation, block scalars (`|`, `>`), anchors and wrong value types are
config errors (exit 2, one generic line on stderr).

Channel of a note (first 30 lines only; values folded: lower case, accents
stripped; parenthetical asides ignored; a channel name matches as a whole
token, `-` and word characters being part of the token; a word whose
name_hashes entry exists counts as that channel):
    1. a `channel: <value>` line (also `- **channel:** <value>`);
    2. a quoted `'channel:<name>'` / `"channel:<name>"` label;
    3. a `tags: [ ... ]` flow list (search uses it only when 1-2 name none;
       the doctor joins it with 1-2 for check 3);
    4. search only, when 1-3 name none: path_defaults.
Search tags print the channel names joined by `+` (sorted), `?` for none.

Search: ROUTER.md rows first (at most 3), then file hits in *.md, *.yaml,
*.yml, *.txt under the roots. Never read: dot files and dot folders, .git,
node_modules, bin/, the router file, names matching *.env, .env*, *secret*,
*token*, *credential*; without --raw also *raw*, _tmp/, raw/ and the
raw_roots. Ignore files (.gitignore and friends) are not honoured, symlinks
are not followed, files over 2 MiB and files holding a NUL byte (binary) are
not searched. A query term matches at the start of a word, ignoring case and
accents on Latin letters; at most 40 matching lines count per file. A line
that looks like a credential is printed as
`[line withheld: looks like a credential]`.
Engines: `rg` (ripgrep, used only if already on PATH) and `python` (pure
Python, never spawns rg); both give the same ranked output: rg only finds
the candidate lines, the deny rules, ranking and printing are shared Python
code. --engine wins over $SB_ENGINE; `auto` (default) picks rg when it is
on PATH, else python. --engine rg without rg on PATH is a usage error.
--channel X is strict: only notes whose channel is exactly X; untagged and
mixed notes are withheld and counted.

Search output:
    sb "<query>"[ --channel X]: <r> router + <k> of <n> file hits, <t> ms, engine <rg|python>[, <w> withheld by channel filter]
    R [<ch>] <topic> -> <paths> | <description>
    <i> [<channel or ?>] <path relative to home>[:<line>]  <best line or (path match)>
    no hits: not in the second brain.
Exit codes: 0 = search ran (hits or none), 2 = usage or config error
(unknown flag, no query terms, --channel not configured, bad --engine, an
unusable scan key while name_hashes has entries).

Doctor (--doctor; never spawns rg): notes are *.md files below a folder of
home (files directly in home, such as README.md and the router file, are
not notes), under the roots, with the search deny rules applied (raw roots
and raw rules excluded). Checks (second-brain/DOCTOR-SPEC.md):
    1 a router path does not exist (or the router file is missing)  exit 1
    2 a note has no `channel:` line, no channel label and no
      configured channel in tags (path defaults do not count)       exit 3
    3 channel and tags together name more than one channel           exit 3
    4 a note with one channel sits in a folder that disagrees: the
      path default for its path, or else its first folder, is not
      its channel                                                    exit 3
    5 a `links:` entry (flow or block list) or a `[[target|label]]`
      / `[[target#anchor]]` link resolves (path from home, path from
      the note's folder, `.md` optional, or a unique file stem) to a
      note whose channel is not the linking note's; unresolved links
      are ignored; one line per linking note                        exit 3
    6 a router row does not name exactly one configured channel, or
      one of its paths sits outside that channel's folder (the path
      default for the path, or else its first folder, is not the
      row's channel)                                                 exit 3
    7 a folder directly holding notes is not covered by a router path
      (that folder or an ancestor)                                   warn
    8 a line looks like an email address, a phone number (9 to 15
      digits with the usual separators), an IBAN, or a date next to
      a birth keyword (born, DOB, date of birth); plain dates, times,
      prices, versions and note ids do not count (heuristic)         warn
    9 a token of the `channel:` value (split on , + / | and spaces,
      asides dropped) or a `'channel:<name>'` label is not in channels
      (a word with a name_hashes entry counts as its channel)        exit 3
    Checks 4 and 5 use the note's channel set from its `channel:` line,
    label and tags together: a note with several channels (check 3) or
    none (check 2) is not folder-checked, and a link counts as cross-channel
    when the linked note names a channel the linking note does not.
Doctor output: one line per finding, sorted by check then path:
    FAIL <check> <path>      (WARN for 7, 8 and disabled fail_on_* checks)
    sb doctor: <n> notes, <r> router rows, <f> failures, <w> warnings
Paths are relative to home (folders end with `/`; checks 1 and 6 print the
router path as written). The matching line is never printed.
Exit code: 3 if a check of exit 3 failed, else 1 if check 1 failed, else 0.

Scan key (name_hashes): 32 random bytes in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/grok-kit/scan.key
(an absolute XDG_CONFIG_HOME only), else ~/.config/grok-kit/scan.key; file
mode 0600, folder mode 0700, outside every repo; never printed.
    --init-key      creates it (folder made 0700 when missing; an existing
                    folder open to group or others, or an existing key, is
                    refused); prints the path. Reads no config.
    --hash-name     prints the name hash of each non-blank stdin line, in
                    order; each line must be one word of letters and digits
                    (folded); otherwise exit 2, nothing printed and the line
                    never echoed. Needs the key; reads no config.
Both take no other arguments (--config is ignored). With name_hashes
entries, search and --doctor read the key first and fail closed (exit 2, one
line naming the file and `sb --init-key`) when it is missing, unreadable, a
symlink, not a regular file, another user's, open to group or others, or not
32 bytes; there is no unkeyed fallback. Rotation: a new key invalidates every
entry; delete the key, run --init-key and re-hash the plain words with
--hash-name (unkeyed sha256 entries of older kits must be re-hashed too).

Read-only: sb never writes, moves or deletes anything; the one exception is
--init-key, which creates only the scan key. Stdlib only, Python 3.9+.
"""

import errno
import fnmatch
import hashlib
import hmac
import os
import re
import secrets
import shutil
import stat
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import unicodedata


class ConfigError(Exception):
    """A malformed or invalid kit.config.yaml (exit 2)."""


class UsageError(Exception):
    """A bad command line (exit 2)."""


class ScanKeyError(Exception):
    """A missing or unusable scan key, or a refused --init-key (exit 2)."""


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- defaults

DEFAULT_HOME = "${HOME}/second-brain"
DEFAULT_ROUTER = "ROUTER.md"
DEFAULT_CHANNELS = ("dance-school", "other-activities")
DOCTOR_FLAGS = (
    "fail_on_untagged", "fail_on_multiple_channels", "fail_on_folder_mismatch",
    "fail_on_cross_channel_link", "fail_on_missing_router_path",
)
CONFIG_NAME = "kit.config.yaml"

GLOBS = ("*.md", "*.yaml", "*.yml", "*.txt")
DENY_NAMES = ("*.env", ".env*", "*secret*", "*token*", "*credential*")
DENY_DIRS = ("node_modules", "bin")
RAW_NAMES = ("*raw*",)
RAW_DIRS = ("_tmp", "raw")
MAX_FILESIZE = 2 * 1024 * 1024
MAX_COUNT = 40
HEAD_LINES = 30
HEAD_LINE_CHARS = 4096
DEFAULT_LIMIT = 8
ENGINES = ("auto", "rg", "python")

SECRET_RE = re.compile(r"(sk-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,}|gh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}|github_pat_|xox[abprs]-|"
                       r"AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}|-----BEGIN [A-Z ]*PRIVATE KEY|eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}\.|"
                       r"(?i:(password|passwd|api[_-]?key|secret|token|bearer)\s*[:=]\s*['\"]?[A-Za-z0-9_\-/+]{8,}))")
STOP = set("the a an and or of for to in on at is are was what where how when who my his her with about from".split())
CHANNEL_FORBIDDEN = re.compile(r"[\s,+|/\[\]\"']")
HASH_KEY_RE = re.compile(r"[0-9a-fA-F]{16}")
NAME_WORD_RE = re.compile(r"[^\W_]+")

KEY_DIR = "grok-kit"
KEY_FILE = "scan.key"
KEY_BYTES = 32
KEY_HINT = "create it once with: sb --init-key"


def fold(s):
    return "".join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize("NFKD", s.lower()) if not unicodedata.combining(c))


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- scan key

def name_hash(key, word):
    """The name_hashes key of a folded word: the first 16 hex chars of
    HMAC-SHA256(scan key, word)."""
    return hmac.new(key, word.encode("utf-8"), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()[:16]


def scan_key_path(environ):
    """$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/grok-kit/scan.key (an absolute XDG_CONFIG_HOME only,
    as the XDG spec says), else $HOME/.config/grok-kit/scan.key."""
    base = environ.get("XDG_CONFIG_HOME") or ""
    if not os.path.isabs(base):
        home = environ.get("HOME") or ""
        if not os.path.isabs(home):
            raise ScanKeyError("the scan key lives under $HOME/.config, but HOME is not set; set HOME, then "
                               + KEY_HINT)
        base = os.path.join(home, ".config")
    return os.path.join(base, KEY_DIR, KEY_FILE)


def _private_mode(st):
    return not stat.S_IMODE(st.st_mode) & 0o077


def _owned(st):
    return not hasattr(os, "getuid") or st.st_uid == os.getuid()


def read_scan_key(environ):
    """The key bytes. Fails closed (ScanKeyError) when the file is missing or
    unreadable, is a symlink or not a regular file, belongs to another user,
    is open to group or others, or does not hold exactly 32 bytes. The bytes
    are never printed."""
    path = scan_key_path(environ)
    flags = os.O_RDONLY | getattr(os, "O_NOFOLLOW", 0) | getattr(os, "O_NONBLOCK", 0)
    try:
        fd = os.open(path, flags)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        raise ScanKeyError("second_brain.name_hashes needs the scan key %s, which does not exist; %s"
                           % (path, KEY_HINT))
    except OSError as exc:
        why = "is a symlink, which is refused" if exc.errno == errno.ELOOP else "cannot be read"
        raise ScanKeyError("the scan key %s %s; delete it and %s" % (path, why, KEY_HINT))
    try:
        st = os.fstat(fd)
        if not stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode):
            raise ScanKeyError("the scan key %s is not a regular file; remove it and %s" % (path, KEY_HINT))
        if not _owned(st):
            raise ScanKeyError("the scan key %s belongs to another user; delete it and %s" % (path, KEY_HINT))
        if not _private_mode(st):
            raise ScanKeyError("the scan key %s is open to other users; run chmod 600 on it if only you ever "
                               "had access, else delete it, %s and re-hash name_hashes" % (path, KEY_HINT))
        data = b""
        while len(data) <= KEY_BYTES:
            chunk = os.read(fd, KEY_BYTES + 1 - len(data))
            if not chunk:
                break
            data += chunk
    except OSError:
        raise ScanKeyError("the scan key %s cannot be read; delete it and %s" % (path, KEY_HINT))
    finally:
        os.close(fd)
    if len(data) != KEY_BYTES:
        raise ScanKeyError("the scan key %s is not a %d-byte key; delete it, %s and re-hash name_hashes"
                           % (path, KEY_BYTES, KEY_HINT))
    return data


def _make_private_dir(path):
    """Create path with mode 0700 (missing parents with the default mode);
    an existing folder is left as it is. True if it was created."""
    try:
        os.mkdir(path, 0o700)
    except FileExistsError:
        return False
    except FileNotFoundError:
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)
        return _make_private_dir(path)
    os.chmod(path, 0o700)  # the umask can only have narrowed it
    return True


def init_scan_key(environ):
    """Create the scan key: 32 bytes from the OS CSPRNG in a new file of mode
    0600, in a folder of mode 0700 (created so when missing; an existing one
    open to others is refused, never chmod-ed). The file appears complete in
    one step (written to a temp name, then hard-linked); an existing key is
    never replaced. Returns the path."""
    path = scan_key_path(environ)
    folder = os.path.dirname(path)
    if os.path.lexists(path):
        raise ScanKeyError("the scan key %s already exists; to rotate it, delete it first, then run sb --init-key "
                           "and re-hash name_hashes (see second-brain/bin/README.md)" % path)
    try:
        _make_private_dir(os.path.dirname(folder))
        _make_private_dir(folder)
        st = os.stat(folder)
    except OSError:
        raise ScanKeyError("the key folder %s cannot be created" % folder)
    if not stat.S_ISDIR(st.st_mode) or not _owned(st):
        raise ScanKeyError("the key folder %s is not a folder of yours" % folder)
    if not _private_mode(st):
        raise ScanKeyError("the key folder %s is open to other users; run chmod 700 on it, then sb --init-key"
                           % folder)
    tmp = os.path.join(folder, ".%s.%s.tmp" % (KEY_FILE, secrets.token_hex(8)))
    try:
        fd = os.open(tmp, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | getattr(os, "O_NOFOLLOW", 0), 0o600)
        try:
            os.fchmod(fd, 0o600)
            view = memoryview(secrets.token_bytes(KEY_BYTES))
            while view:
                view = view[os.write(fd, view):]
            os.fsync(fd)
        finally:
            os.close(fd)
        os.link(tmp, path)
    except FileExistsError:
        raise ScanKeyError("the scan key %s already exists; it was not replaced" % path)
    except OSError:
        raise ScanKeyError("the scan key %s cannot be created" % path)
    finally:
        try:
            os.unlink(tmp)
        except OSError:
            pass
    return path


def hash_names(key, text):
    """The name hash of each non-blank line of text, in order. Each line must
    be one word (letters and digits, folded like note values); a line that is
    not is refused without echoing it, and nothing is returned."""
    out = []
    for n, line in enumerate(text.splitlines(), 1):
        word = fold(line).strip()
        if not word:
            continue
        if not NAME_WORD_RE.fullmatch(word):
            raise UsageError("sb: line %d is not one word (letters and digits only); nothing was printed" % n)
        out.append(name_hash(key, word))
    return out


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- YAML subset

_NESTED = object()
_INT_RE = re.compile(r"[-+]?[0-9]+")
_TRUE = ("true", "True", "TRUE")
_FALSE = ("false", "False", "FALSE")
_NULL = ("null", "Null", "NULL", "~")
_DQ_ESCAPES = {'"': '"', "\\": "\\", "/": "/", "n": "\n", "t": "\t", "r": "\r", "0": "\0"}
_PLAIN_BAD_START = "|>&*!%@`]},?"


def _err(lineno, reason):
    return ConfigError("line %d: %s" % (lineno, reason))


def _parse_double(s, i, lineno):
    out, j, n = [], i + 1, len(s)
    while j < n:
        c = s[j]
        if c == '"':
            return "".join(out), j + 1
        if c == "\\":
            if j + 1 >= n:
                break
            e = s[j + 1]
            if e in _DQ_ESCAPES:
                out.append(_DQ_ESCAPES[e])
                j += 2
                continue
            width = {"x": 2, "u": 4, "U": 8}.get(e)
            digits = s[j + 2:j + 2 + width] if width else ""
            if not width or not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-fA-F]{%d}" % width, digits):
                raise _err(lineno, "unknown escape in a double-quoted scalar")
            out.append(chr(int(digits, 16)))
            j += 2 + width
            continue
        out.append(c)
        j += 1
    raise _err(lineno, "unterminated double-quoted scalar")


def _parse_single(s, i, lineno):
    out, j, n = [], i + 1, len(s)
    while j < n:
        c = s[j]
        if c == "'":
            if j + 1 < n and s[j + 1] == "'":
                out.append("'")
                j += 2
                continue
            return "".join(out), j + 1
        out.append(c)
        j += 1
    raise _err(lineno, "unterminated single-quoted scalar")


def _resolve_plain(token, lineno):
    if not token:
        raise _err(lineno, "empty value")
    if token[0] in _PLAIN_BAD_START or token.startswith("- ") or token == "-":
        raise _err(lineno, "unsupported YAML syntax (block scalar, anchor, alias, tag or nested block)")
    if ": " in token or token.endswith(":") or " #" in token:
        raise _err(lineno, "unexpected ':' or '#' in a plain scalar")
    if token in _TRUE:
        return True
    if token in _FALSE:
        return False
    if token in _NULL:
        return None
    if _INT_RE.fullmatch(token):
        return int(token)
    return token


def _skip_ws(s, j):
    while j < len(s) and s[j] in " \t":
        j += 1
    return j


def _expect_end(s, j, lineno):
    j = _skip_ws(s, j)
    if j < len(s) and s[j] != "#":
        raise _err(lineno, "unexpected text after a value")


def _flow_scalar(s, j, lineno, stops):
    """A quoted or plain scalar inside a flow collection; returns (value, j)."""
    if j < len(s) and s[j] == '"':
        return _parse_double(s, j, lineno)
    if j < len(s) and s[j] == "'":
        return _parse_single(s, j, lineno)
    k = j
    while k < len(s) and s[k] not in stops:
        if s[k] in "[{":
            raise _err(lineno, "nested flow collections are not supported")
        k += 1
    if k >= len(s):
        raise _err(lineno, "unterminated flow collection")
    return _resolve_plain(s[j:k].strip(), lineno), k


def _parse_flow_seq(s, i, lineno):
    items, j = [], _skip_ws(s, i + 1)
    if j < len(s) and s[j] == "]":
        return items, j + 1
    while True:
        j = _skip_ws(s, j)
        if j < len(s) and s[j] == "]" and items:  # trailing comma
            return items, j + 1
        value, j = _flow_scalar(s, j, lineno, ",]")
        items.append(value)
        j = _skip_ws(s, j)
        if j >= len(s):
            raise _err(lineno, "unterminated flow list")
        if s[j] == "]":
            return items, j + 1
        if s[j] != ",":
            raise _err(lineno, "expected ',' or ']' in a flow list")
        j += 1


def _parse_flow_map(s, i, lineno):
    result, j = {}, _skip_ws(s, i + 1)
    if j < len(s) and s[j] == "}":
        return result, j + 1
    while True:
        j = _skip_ws(s, j)
        if j < len(s) and s[j] == "}" and result:  # trailing comma
            return result, j + 1
        key, j = _flow_scalar(s, j, lineno, ":,}")
        j = _skip_ws(s, j)
        if j >= len(s) or s[j] != ":":
            raise _err(lineno, "expected ':' in a flow mapping")
        if not isinstance(key, str) or key in result:
            raise _err(lineno, "bad or duplicate key in a flow mapping")
        value, j = _flow_scalar(s, _skip_ws(s, j + 1), lineno, ",}")
        result[key] = value
        j = _skip_ws(s, j)
        if j >= len(s):
            raise _err(lineno, "unterminated flow mapping")
        if s[j] == "}":
            return result, j + 1
        if s[j] != ",":
            raise _err(lineno, "expected ',' or '}' in a flow mapping")
        j += 1


def _parse_value(s, lineno, scalars_only=False):
    """The value text after `key:` or `- `; _NESTED when it is empty."""
    s = s.strip(" \t")
    if not s or s.startswith("#"):
        return _NESTED
    head = s[0]
    if head in "[{" and scalars_only:
        raise _err(lineno, "block list items must be scalars")
    if head == '"':
        value, j = _parse_double(s, 0, lineno)
    elif head == "'":
        value, j = _parse_single(s, 0, lineno)
    elif head == "[":
        value, j = _parse_flow_seq(s, 0, lineno)
    elif head == "{":
        value, j = _parse_flow_map(s, 0, lineno)
    else:
        cut = re.search(r"[ \t]#", s)
        return _resolve_plain((s[:cut.start()] if cut else s).rstrip(" \t"), lineno)
    _expect_end(s, j, lineno)
    return value


def _is_item(text):
    return text == "-" or text.startswith("- ")


def _split_key(text, lineno):
    if text[0] in "\"'":
        key, j = (_parse_double if text[0] == '"' else _parse_single)(text, 0, lineno)
        j = _skip_ws(text, j)
        if j >= len(text) or text[j] != ":" or (j + 1 < len(text) and text[j + 1] not in " \t"):
            raise _err(lineno, "expected ':' after a quoted key")
        return key, text[j + 1:]
    m = re.search(r":(?:[ \t]|$)", text)
    if not m:
        raise _err(lineno, "expected 'key: value'")
    key = text[:m.start()].rstrip(" \t")
    if not key or key[0] in "#[]{},&*!|>%@`?" or re.search(r"[ \t]#", key):
        raise _err(lineno, "bad key")
    return key, text[m.end():]


def _parse_list(lines, i, indent):
    items = []
    while i < len(lines):
        lineno, ind, text = lines[i]
        if ind < indent or (ind == indent and not _is_item(text)):
            break
        if ind > indent:
            raise _err(lineno, "unexpected indentation")
        value = _parse_value(text[1:], lineno, scalars_only=True)
        if value is _NESTED:
            raise _err(lineno, "block list items must be scalars")
        items.append(value)
        i += 1
    return items, i


def _parse_mapping(lines, i, indent):
    result = {}
    while i < len(lines):
        lineno, ind, text = lines[i]
        if ind < indent:
            break
        if ind > indent:
            raise _err(lineno, "unexpected indentation")
        if _is_item(text):
            raise _err(lineno, "a list item where a key was expected")
        key, rest = _split_key(text, lineno)
        if key in result:
            raise _err(lineno, "duplicate key")
        value = _parse_value(rest, lineno)
        i += 1
        if value is _NESTED:
            value = None
            if i < len(lines) and lines[i][1] > indent:
                value, i = _parse_block(lines, i, lines[i][1])
            elif i < len(lines) and lines[i][1] == indent and _is_item(lines[i][2]):
                value, i = _parse_list(lines, i, indent)
        result[key] = value
    return result, i


def _parse_block(lines, i, indent):
    if _is_item(lines[i][2]):
        return _parse_list(lines, i, indent)
    return _parse_mapping(lines, i, indent)


def parse_config_text(text):
    """Parse the YAML subset above into nested dicts, lists and scalars."""
    if text[:1] == chr(0xFEFF):  # a UTF-8 byte order mark
        text = text[1:]
    lines = []
    for lineno, raw in enumerate(text.split("\n"), 1):
        raw = raw.rstrip("\r")
        content = raw.lstrip(" \t")
        if not content or content.startswith("#"):
            continue
        lead = raw[:len(raw) - len(content)]
        if "\t" in lead:
            raise _err(lineno, "tab in indentation")
        lines.append((lineno, len(lead), content.rstrip(" \t")))
    if not lines:
        return {}
    if _is_item(lines[0][2]):
        raise _err(lines[0][0], "the top level must be a mapping")
    result, i = _parse_mapping(lines, 0, lines[0][1])
    if i < len(lines):
        raise _err(lines[i][0], "unexpected indentation")
    return result


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- settings

_VAR_RE = re.compile(r"\$\{([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\}")


def _expand_path(value, environ, base_dir, what, fallbacks=None):
    def sub(m):
        name = m.group(1)
        if environ.get(name):
            return environ[name]
        if fallbacks and name in fallbacks:
            return fallbacks[name]()
        raise ConfigError("%s names an unset variable" % what)

    if not isinstance(value, str) or not value:
        raise ConfigError("%s must be a non-empty string" % what)
    path = _VAR_RE.sub(sub, value)
    if "${" in _VAR_RE.sub("", value):
        raise ConfigError("%s has a malformed ${VAR}" % what)
    if path == "~" or path.startswith("~/"):
        if not environ.get("HOME"):
            raise ConfigError("%s needs HOME" % what)
        path = environ["HOME"] + path[1:]
    if not os.path.isabs(path):
        path = os.path.join(base_dir or os.getcwd(), path)
    return os.path.normpath(path)


def _find_config(config_path, environ):
    if config_path:
        if not os.path.isfile(config_path):
            raise ConfigError("config file not found (--config)")
        return config_path
    if environ.get("KIT_CONFIG"):
        if not os.path.isfile(environ["KIT_CONFIG"]):
            raise ConfigError("config file not found ($KIT_CONFIG)")
        return environ["KIT_CONFIG"]
    candidates = []
    if environ.get("KIT_HOME"):
        candidates.append(os.path.join(environ["KIT_HOME"], CONFIG_NAME))
    if environ.get("HOME"):
        candidates.append(os.path.join(environ["HOME"], "grok-kit", CONFIG_NAME))
    for path in candidates:
        if os.path.isfile(path):
            return path
    return None


def _inside_relative(value, what):
    """A path relative to home that stays inside it."""
    if not isinstance(value, str) or not value.strip():
        raise ConfigError("%s entries must be non-empty strings" % what)
    norm = os.path.normpath(value)
    if os.path.isabs(value) or norm == ".." or norm.startswith(".." + os.sep):
        raise ConfigError("%s entries must be relative paths inside home" % what)
    return value


def _string_list(block, key, default):
    value = block.get(key)
    if value is None:
        return list(default)
    if not isinstance(value, list):
        raise ConfigError("second_brain.%s must be a list" % key)
    return [_inside_relative(v, "second_brain." + key) for v in value]


def _channels(block):
    value = block.get("channels")
    if value is None:
        return list(DEFAULT_CHANNELS)
    if not isinstance(value, list) or not value:
        raise ConfigError("second_brain.channels must be a non-empty list")
    seen = set()
    for name in value:
        if not isinstance(name, str) or not name or CHANNEL_FORBIDDEN.search(name):
            raise ConfigError("second_brain.channels holds a bad channel name")
        if fold(name) in seen:
            raise ConfigError("second_brain.channels holds a duplicate")
        seen.add(fold(name))
    return list(value)


def _channel_map(block, key, channels, key_check):
    value = block.get(key)
    if value is None:
        return None
    if not isinstance(value, dict):
        raise ConfigError("second_brain.%s must be a mapping" % key)
    out = {}
    for k, v in value.items():
        k = key_check(k)
        if v not in channels:
            raise ConfigError("second_brain.%s maps to a channel that is not configured" % key)
        out[k] = v
    return out


def _prefix_key(k):
    if not isinstance(k, str) or not k.strip():
        raise ConfigError("second_brain.path_defaults keys must be non-empty strings")
    return k


def _hash_key(k):
    if not isinstance(k, str) or not HASH_KEY_RE.fullmatch(k):
        raise ConfigError("second_brain.name_hashes keys must be 16 hex characters")
    return k.lower()


def _doctor_flags(block):
    value = block.get("doctor")
    flags = dict((name, True) for name in DOCTOR_FLAGS)
    if value is None:
        return flags
    if not isinstance(value, dict):
        raise ConfigError("second_brain.doctor must be a mapping")
    for name, flag in value.items():
        if name not in flags:
            raise ConfigError("second_brain.doctor has an unknown flag")
        if not isinstance(flag, bool):
            raise ConfigError("second_brain.doctor flags must be true or false")
        flags[name] = flag
    return flags


def load_settings(config_path=None, environ=None):
    """Resolve the second_brain settings (see the docstring) into a dict with
    the keys home, router_file, channels, roots, raw_roots, path_defaults,
    name_hashes, boost_paths, doctor and config_path."""
    environ = os.environ if environ is None else environ
    path = _find_config(config_path, environ)
    data = {}
    if path is not None:
        try:
            with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                data = parse_config_text(fh.read())
        except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError):
            raise ConfigError("config file cannot be read as UTF-8 text")
    base_dir = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(path)) if path else None
    block = data.get("second_brain")
    if block is None:
        block = {}
    if not isinstance(block, dict):
        raise ConfigError("second_brain must be a mapping")

    def kit_home():
        kit = data.get("kit")
        if not isinstance(kit, dict) or not kit.get("home"):
            raise ConfigError("second_brain.home names an unset variable")
        return _expand_path(kit["home"], environ, base_dir, "kit.home")

    if environ.get("SB_HOME"):
        home = _expand_path(environ["SB_HOME"], environ, None, "SB_HOME")
    else:
        home = _expand_path(block.get("home") or DEFAULT_HOME, environ, base_dir,
                            "second_brain.home", {"KIT_HOME": kit_home})
    router_file = block.get("router_file")
    router_file = DEFAULT_ROUTER if router_file is None else _inside_relative(router_file, "second_brain.router_file")
    channels = _channels(block)
    path_defaults = _channel_map(block, "path_defaults", channels, _prefix_key)
    if path_defaults is None:
        path_defaults = dict((name + "/", name) for name in channels)
    name_hashes = _channel_map(block, "name_hashes", channels, _hash_key) or {}
    boost = block.get("boost_paths")
    if boost is not None and (not isinstance(boost, list) or not all(isinstance(b, str) and b for b in boost)):
        raise ConfigError("second_brain.boost_paths must be a list of path prefixes")
    return {
        "home": home,
        "router_file": router_file,
        "channels": channels,
        "roots": _string_list(block, "roots", ["."]),
        "raw_roots": _string_list(block, "raw_roots", []),
        "path_defaults": path_defaults,
        "name_hashes": name_hashes,
        "boost_paths": list(boost or []),
        "doctor": _doctor_flags(block),
        "config_path": path,
    }


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- query terms

def _fold_classes():
    """Base letter -> the Latin letters that fold to it, for accent-tolerant
    term patterns (`cafe` finds `Cafe` with an accent)."""
    classes = {}
    for cp in list(range(0xC0, 0x250)) + list(range(0x1E00, 0x1F00)):
        ch = chr(cp)
        base = fold(ch)
        if len(base) == 1 and "a" <= base <= "z" and ch != base:
            classes.setdefault(base, []).append(ch)
    return dict((base, "[" + base + "".join(chars) + "]") for base, chars in classes.items())


FOLD_CLASSES = _fold_classes()
# Escaped in both Python re and the Rust regex syntax rg uses.
REGEX_META = set("\\.+*?()|[]{}^$#&-~")


def terms_of(q):
    out = []
    for w in re.findall(r"[\w.+-]+", fold(q)):
        w = w.strip(".-")
        if len(w) < 2 or w in STOP:
            continue
        if len(w) > 4 and w.endswith("s") and not w.endswith("ss"):
            w = w[:-1]
        if w not in out:
            out.append(w)
    return out


def term_re(t):
    """Word-start anchored and accent tolerant; valid for both engines."""
    return r"\b" + "".join(FOLD_CLASSES.get(c) or ("\\" + c if c in REGEX_META else c) for c in t)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the brain

def _join(rel_dir, name):
    return name if rel_dir in ("", ".") else rel_dir + "/" + name


def _under(rel, prefixes):
    for p in prefixes:
        p = os.path.normpath(p).replace(os.sep, "/")
        if p == "." or rel == p or rel.startswith(p + "/"):
            return True
    return False


def _relnorm(path):
    return os.path.normpath(path).replace(os.sep, "/")


def tag(c):
    return "+".join(sorted(c)) if c else "?"


class Brain:
    """The configured note tree: deny rules, the walker, channels, router."""

    def __init__(self, settings):
        self.s = settings
        self.home = settings["home"]
        self.channels = list(settings["channels"])
        self.router_rel = _relnorm(settings["router_file"])
        self.channel_res = [
            (name, re.compile(r"(?<![\w-])" + re.escape(fold(name)) + r"(?![\w-])"))
            for name in self.channels
        ]
        self.by_fold = dict((fold(name), name) for name in self.channels)
        self.name_hashes = settings["name_hashes"]
        self.name_key = settings.get("name_key")
        if self.name_hashes and self.name_key is None:
            raise ScanKeyError("second_brain.name_hashes needs the scan key; " + KEY_HINT)
        self.path_defaults = sorted(
            ((_relnorm(p), ch) for p, ch in settings["path_defaults"].items()),
            key=lambda item: -len(item[0]),
        )
        self._info = {}

    # -- deny rules

    def denied(self, rel, raw, is_dir=False):
        parts = rel.split("/")
        last = len(parts) - 1
        for i, part in enumerate(parts):
            low = part.lower()
            if part.startswith("."):
                return True
            names = DENY_NAMES + (() if raw else RAW_NAMES)
            if any(fnmatch.fnmatchcase(low, g) for g in names):
                return True
            if i < last or is_dir:
                if low in DENY_DIRS or (not raw and low in RAW_DIRS):
                    return True
        if not is_dir and rel.lower() == self.router_rel.lower():
            return True
        return not raw and _under(rel, self.s["raw_roots"])

    def eligible(self, rel, raw):
        """A file sb may read: allowed name, regular (no symlink), <= 2 MiB."""
        if not any(fnmatch.fnmatchcase(rel.rsplit("/", 1)[-1], g) for g in GLOBS):
            return False
        if self.denied(rel, raw):
            return False
        try:
            st = os.lstat(os.path.join(self.home, rel))
        except OSError:
            return False
        return stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode) and st.st_size <= MAX_FILESIZE

    def search_roots(self, raw):
        """Existing roots as normalized relative paths, raw roots last."""
        out = []
        for root in self.s["roots"] + (self.s["raw_roots"] if raw else []):
            rel = _relnorm(root)
            full = os.path.join(self.home, rel)
            if rel != "." and os.path.islink(full):
                continue
            if os.path.isdir(full) or os.path.isfile(full):
                if rel not in out:
                    out.append(rel)
        return out

    def walk(self, roots, raw):
        """The eligible files under roots, each once (the python engine's
        file list and the doctor's)."""
        seen, out = set(), []

        def add(rel):
            if rel not in seen and self.eligible(rel, raw):
                seen.add(rel)
                out.append(rel)

        for root in roots:
            full = os.path.join(self.home, root)
            if os.path.isfile(full):
                add(root)
                continue
            for dirpath, dirnames, filenames in os.walk(full):
                rel_dir = _relnorm(os.path.relpath(dirpath, self.home))
                dirnames[:] = sorted(
                    d for d in dirnames
                    if not os.path.islink(os.path.join(dirpath, d))
                    and not self.denied(_join(rel_dir, d), raw, is_dir=True)
                )
                for name in sorted(filenames):
                    add(_join(rel_dir, name))
        return out

    # -- channels

    def chans_from_text(self, v):
        v = re.sub(r"\([^)]*\)", " ", v)  # parenthetical asides don't tag
        f = fold(v)
        c = set(name for name, rx in self.channel_res if rx.search(f))
        if self.name_hashes:
            for w in NAME_WORD_RE.findall(f):
                hit = self.name_hashes.get(name_hash(self.name_key, w))
                if hit:
                    c.add(hit)
        return c

    def head(self, rel):
        lines = []
        try:
            with open(os.path.join(self.home, rel), encoding="utf-8", errors="ignore") as fh:
                for _ in range(HEAD_LINES):
                    ln = fh.readline(HEAD_LINE_CHARS)
                    if not ln:
                        break
                    lines.append(ln.rstrip("\n"))
        except OSError:
            pass
        return lines

    def channel_info(self, rel):
        """{'line': bool, 'explicit': set, 'labelled': bool, 'tags': set or None,
        'unknown': int} from the first lines of a note; `unknown` counts the
        channel tokens (of `channel:` lines and labels) that name no
        configured channel (doctor check 9)."""
        if rel in self._info:
            return self._info[rel]
        info = {"line": False, "explicit": set(), "labelled": False, "tags": None, "unknown": 0}
        for ln in self.head(rel):
            m = re.match(r"^\s*[-*>]*\s*\**channel\**\s*:\s*\**\s*(.+)", ln, re.I)
            if m:
                info["line"] = True
                info["explicit"] |= self.chans_from_text(m.group(1))
                info["unknown"] += sum(1 for t in self.channel_tokens(m.group(1)) if not self.chans_from_text(t))
                continue
            m = re.search(r"['\"]channel:([^'\"\s]+)['\"]", ln, re.I)
            if m:
                info["labelled"] = True
                name = self.by_fold.get(fold(m.group(1)))
                if name:
                    info["explicit"].add(name)
                else:
                    info["unknown"] += 1
                continue
            m = re.match(r"^tags:\s*\[(.*)\]", ln)
            if m and info["tags"] is None:
                info["tags"] = self.chans_from_text(m.group(1))
        self._info[rel] = info
        return info

    @staticmethod
    def channel_tokens(value):
        """The tokens of a `channel:` value: asides, quotes, bold markers and
        a trailing comment dropped, split on , + / | and spaces."""
        value = re.sub(r"\([^)]*\)", " ", value)
        value = re.split(r"\s#", value)[0]
        return [t.strip("\"'*`") for t in re.split(r"[,+/|\s]+", value) if t.strip("\"'*`")]

    def doctor_channels(self, rel):
        """The doctor's channel set of a note: `channel:` lines, labels and
        tags together (path defaults do not count)."""
        info = self.channel_info(rel)
        return set(info["explicit"]) | set(info["tags"] or ())

    def folder_channel(self, rel):
        """The channel a path's folder claims: its path default, else its
        first folder (checks 4 and 6)."""
        default = self.path_default(rel)
        if default:
            return default
        first = rel.split("/", 1)[0]
        return self.by_fold.get(fold(first)) or first

    def path_default(self, rel):
        for prefix, ch in self.path_defaults:
            if prefix == "." or rel == prefix or rel.startswith(prefix + "/"):
                return ch
        return None

    def channel(self, rel):
        """The search rule: explicit channel, else tags, else path default."""
        info = self.channel_info(rel)
        c = set(info["explicit"]) or set(info["tags"] or ())
        if not c:
            default = self.path_default(rel)
            if default:
                c = {default}
        return c

    # -- router

    def load_router(self):
        """(rows, found); a row is a dict topic, kw, ch, paths, desc."""
        rows = []
        try:
            with open(os.path.join(self.home, self.router_rel), encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as fh:
                lines = fh.read().splitlines()
        except OSError:
            return rows, False
        for ln in lines:
            if not ln.startswith("|") or ln.startswith("|---"):
                continue
            cells = [x.strip() for x in ln.strip().strip("|").split("|")]
            if len(cells) < 5 or cells[0] == "Topic":
                continue
            topic, kw, ch, paths, desc = cells[:5]
            rows.append(dict(topic=topic, kw=fold(topic + ", " + kw),
                             ch=set(x.strip() for x in ch.split("+") if x.strip()),
                             paths=re.findall(r"`([^`]+)`", paths), desc=desc))
        return rows, True


def allowed(c, want):
    """--channel is strict: exactly the wanted channel, nothing else."""
    return not want or set(c) == {want}


def router_hits(rows, terms, phrase, want):
    out = []
    for r in rows:
        if not allowed(r["ch"], want):
            continue
        n = sum(1 for t in terms if re.search(r"\b" + re.escape(t), r["kw"]))
        if not n:
            continue
        s = n * 10 + (8 if len(terms) > 1 and phrase in r["kw"] else 0) + (5 if n == len(terms) else 0)
        out.append((s, r))
    out.sort(key=lambda x: -x[0])
    return out


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- engines

class EngineError(Exception):
    """rg could not run (exit 2)."""


def _lines_of(data):
    lines = data.split(b"\n")
    if lines and lines[-1] == b"":
        lines.pop()
    return lines


def _read_text_file(path):
    """The bytes of a searchable file, or None (unreadable, too big, binary)."""
    try:
        with open(path, "rb") as fh:
            data = fh.read(MAX_FILESIZE + 1)
    except OSError:
        return None
    if len(data) > MAX_FILESIZE or b"\0" in data:
        return None
    return data


def python_engine(brain, roots, raw, pattern):
    """Pure Python: walk, then match line by line. Never spawns rg."""
    files = brain.walk(roots, raw)
    rx = re.compile(pattern, re.IGNORECASE)
    hits = {}
    for rel in files:
        data = _read_text_file(os.path.join(brain.home, rel))
        if data is None:
            continue
        found = []
        for n, line in enumerate(_lines_of(data), 1):
            text = line.decode("utf-8", "surrogateescape")
            if rx.search(text):
                found.append((n, text))
                if len(found) >= MAX_COUNT:
                    break
        if found:
            hits[rel] = found
    return files, hits


_RG_HIT = re.compile(rb"([^\0]*)\0([0-9]+):([^\n]*)\n")


def rg_engine(brain, roots, raw, pattern, rg):
    """rg lists and matches; every result passes the same eligibility rules
    as the python engine, so rg can only narrow nothing and add nothing."""
    if not roots:
        return [], {}
    common = ["--no-config", "--no-ignore", "--color", "never", "--no-messages",
              "--encoding", "none", "--max-filesize", str(MAX_FILESIZE + 1)]
    for g in GLOBS:
        common += ["-g", g]
    deny = ["!" + g for g in DENY_NAMES] + ["!**/%s/**" % d for d in DENY_DIRS]
    if not raw:
        deny += ["!" + g for g in RAW_NAMES] + ["!**/%s/**" % d for d in RAW_DIRS]
    for g in deny:
        common += ["--iglob", g]
    tail = ["--"] + ["./" + r if r.startswith("-") else r for r in roots]
    files_cmd = [rg, "--files", "--null"] + common + tail
    hits_cmd = [rg, "--ignore-case", "--line-number", "--with-filename", "--no-heading", "--null",
                "--max-count", str(MAX_COUNT), "-e", pattern] + common + tail
    try:
        kw = dict(cwd=brain.home, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)
        files_p = subprocess.Popen(files_cmd, **kw)
        hits_p = subprocess.Popen(hits_cmd, **kw)
    except OSError:
        raise EngineError("sb: rg could not be started; try --engine python")
    listed = files_p.communicate()[0]
    found = hits_p.communicate()[0]
    if files_p.returncode not in (0, 1) and not listed:
        raise EngineError("sb: rg failed (exit %d); try --engine python" % files_p.returncode)

    def rel_of(raw_path):
        return _relnorm(raw_path.decode("utf-8", "surrogateescape"))

    files, seen = [], set()
    for raw_path in listed.split(b"\0"):
        if raw_path:
            rel = rel_of(raw_path)
            if rel not in seen and brain.eligible(rel, raw):
                seen.add(rel)
                files.append(rel)
    hits, lines_seen, binary = {}, set(), {}
    for m in _RG_HIT.finditer(found):
        rel, n = rel_of(m.group(1)), int(m.group(2))
        if rel not in seen or (rel, n) in lines_seen:
            continue
        if rel not in binary:  # rg may print lines before a late NUL byte
            binary[rel] = _read_text_file(os.path.join(brain.home, rel)) is None
        if binary[rel]:
            continue
        found_lines = hits.setdefault(rel, [])
        if len(found_lines) < MAX_COUNT:
            lines_seen.add((rel, n))
            found_lines.append((n, m.group(3).decode("utf-8", "surrogateescape")))
    for rel in hits:
        hits[rel].sort()
    return files, hits


def pick_engine(flag, environ):
    choice = flag or environ.get("SB_ENGINE") or "auto"
    if choice not in ENGINES:
        raise UsageError("sb: --engine must be auto, rg or python")
    rg = shutil.which("rg", path=environ.get("PATH", os.defpath))
    if choice == "rg" and not rg:
        raise UsageError("sb: --engine rg needs ripgrep (rg) on PATH; use --engine python")
    if choice == "auto":
        choice = "rg" if rg else "python"
    return choice, rg


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- search

def clean(text):
    """Printable text: invalid UTF-8 bytes dropped."""
    return text.encode("utf-8", "surrogateescape").decode("utf-8", "ignore")


def rank(brain, files, hits, terms, raw, rh):
    """The shared ranking for both engines: [(score, rel, slot)] best first."""
    phrase = " ".join(terms)
    tre = [re.compile(term_re(t), re.I) for t in terms]
    agg = {}

    def slot(f):
        return agg.setdefault(f, {"terms": set(), "pterms": set(), "hits": 0, "best": (-1, 0, "")})

    for f in sorted(hits):
        for n, text in hits[f]:
            ft = fold(text)
            ks = {i for i, r in enumerate(tre) if r.search(ft) or r.search(text)}
            a = slot(f)
            a["hits"] += 1
            a["terms"] |= ks
            sc = len(ks) * 4 + (3 if text.lstrip().startswith("#") else 0) + (5 if len(terms) > 1 and phrase in ft else 0)
            if sc > a["best"][0]:
                a["best"] = (sc, n, text)
    for f in files:  # filename/path matches
        ks = {i for i, r in enumerate(tre) if r.search(fold(f))}
        if ks:
            slot(f)["pterms"] = ks
    routed = {p.rstrip("/") for _, r in rh[:3] for p in r["paths"]}
    boost = brain.s["boost_paths"]
    scored = []
    for f, a in agg.items():
        ct, pt = a["terms"], a["pterms"]
        s = len(ct) * 10 + len(pt) * 6 + (15 if len(ct | pt) == len(terms) else 0) + min(a["hits"], 10) + max(a["best"][0], 0)
        if _under(f, boost):
            s += 4
        if any(f == p or f.startswith(p + "/") for p in routed):
            s += 8
        if raw and (brain.denied(f, False) and not brain.denied(f, True)):
            s -= 6  # raw dumps rank below curated notes
        scored.append((s, f, a))
    scored.sort(key=lambda x: (-x[0], x[1]))
    return scored


def search(settings, query, want, limit, raw, engine, rg, out):
    t0 = time.perf_counter()
    brain = Brain(settings)
    terms = terms_of(query)
    phrase = " ".join(terms)
    roots = brain.search_roots(raw)
    pattern = "|".join(term_re(t) for t in terms)
    if engine == "rg":
        files, hits = rg_engine(brain, roots, raw, pattern, rg)
    else:
        files, hits = python_engine(brain, roots, raw, pattern)
    rows, _ = brain.load_router()
    rh = router_hits(rows, terms, phrase, want)
    withheld, res = 0, []
    for s, f, a in rank(brain, files, hits, terms, raw, rh):
        c = brain.channel(f)
        if allowed(c, want):
            res.append((f, a, c))
        else:
            withheld += 1
    nr = min(3, limit, len(rh))
    nf = max(limit - nr, 0)
    dt = (time.perf_counter() - t0) * 1000
    lines = ['sb "%s"%s: %d router + %d of %d file hits, %.0f ms, engine %s%s' % (
        query, " --channel " + want if want else "", nr, min(nf, len(res)), len(res), dt, engine,
        ", %d withheld by channel filter" % withheld if withheld else "")]
    for _, r in rh[:nr]:
        lines.append("R [%s] %s -> %s | %s" % (tag(r["ch"]), r["topic"], ", ".join(r["paths"]) or "-", r["desc"][:140]))
    for i, (f, a, c) in enumerate(res[:nf], 1):
        _, n, text = a["best"]
        text = " ".join(clean(text).split())
        if SECRET_RE.search(text):
            text = "[line withheld: looks like a credential]"
        loc = clean(f) + (":%d" % n if n else "")
        lines.append("%d [%s] %s  %s" % (i, tag(c), loc, text[:160] if text else "(path match)"))
    if not rh and not res:
        lines.append("no hits: not in the second brain.")
    out.write("\n".join(lines) + "\n")
    return 0


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- doctor

WIKI_LINK_RE = re.compile(r"\[\[([^\]\[]+)\]\]")
LINKS_LINE_RE = re.compile(r"^links\s*:\s*(.*)$")
LIST_ITEM_RE = re.compile(r"^\s+-\s*(.*)$")

EMAIL_HINT_RE = re.compile(r"[\w.+-]+@[\w-]+(?:\.[\w-]+)+")
IBAN_HINT_RE = re.compile(r"(?<![\w-])[A-Z]{2}[0-9]{2}(?: ?[A-Z0-9]){11,30}(?![\w-])")
PHONE_RUN_RE = re.compile(r"(?<![\w.:-])\+?[0-9][0-9 ().-]*[0-9](?![\w:])")
DATE_RE = re.compile(r"\b(?:[0-9]{4}[-./][0-9]{1,2}[-./][0-9]{1,2}|[0-9]{1,2}[-./][0-9]{1,2}[-./][0-9]{2,4}"
                     r"|(?:19|20)[0-9]{2}(?:0[1-9]|1[0-2])(?:0[1-9]|[12][0-9]|3[01]))\b")
BIRTH_RE = re.compile(r"\b(?:born|dob|date of birth|birth ?date|birthday)\b", re.I)


def link_targets(brain, rel, text):
    """The link targets of a note: `links:` entries (a flow list or a block
    list in the first lines) and every `[[target|label]]` / `[[target#anchor]]`
    in the whole text; the label and the anchor are dropped."""
    targets = []
    head = brain.head(rel)
    i = 0
    while i < len(head):
        m = LINKS_LINE_RE.match(head[i])
        i += 1
        if not m:
            continue
        rest = m.group(1).strip()
        if rest.startswith("["):
            flow = re.match(r"\[(.*)\]", rest)
            targets.extend((flow.group(1) if flow else rest[1:]).split(","))
            continue
        if rest and not rest.startswith("#"):
            targets.append(rest)
            continue
        while i < len(head) and LIST_ITEM_RE.match(head[i]):
            targets.append(LIST_ITEM_RE.match(head[i]).group(1))
            i += 1
    targets.extend(WIKI_LINK_RE.findall(text))
    out = []
    for t in targets:
        t = t.strip().strip("\"'").strip()
        if t.startswith("[[") and t.endswith("]]"):
            t = t[2:-2]
        t = t.split("|", 1)[0].split("#", 1)[0].strip()
        if t:
            out.append(t)
    return out


def resolve_link(target, src_dir, note_set, stems):
    """The note a link target names: a path from home, a path from the note's
    folder (`.md` optional), or a unique file stem; None when unresolved."""
    candidates = [_relnorm(target)]
    if src_dir:
        candidates.append(_relnorm(src_dir + "/" + target))
    for c in candidates:
        for variant in (c, c + ".md"):
            if variant in note_set:
                return variant
    stem = target.rsplit("/", 1)[-1]
    if stem.lower().endswith(".md"):
        stem = stem[:-3]
    hits = stems.get(fold(stem), ())
    return hits[0] if len(hits) == 1 else None


def personal_data_hint(line):
    """True when a line looks like an email address, a phone number (9 to 15
    digits with the usual separators, not a date), an IBAN, or a date next
    to a birth keyword. A heuristic; the line itself is never reported."""
    if EMAIL_HINT_RE.search(line) or IBAN_HINT_RE.search(line):
        return True
    if BIRTH_RE.search(line) and DATE_RE.search(line):
        return True
    for m in PHONE_RUN_RE.finditer(line):
        run = m.group(0)
        if DATE_RE.search(run):
            continue
        if 9 <= sum(1 for c in run if c.isdigit()) <= 15:
            return True
    return False


def doctor(settings, out):
    """Checks 1 to 9 (see the docstring); never spawns rg."""
    brain = Brain(settings)
    flags = settings["doctor"]
    rows, found = brain.load_router()
    notes = [f for f in brain.walk(brain.search_roots(False), False) if f.endswith(".md") and "/" in f]
    note_set = set(notes)
    stems = {}
    for f in notes:
        stems.setdefault(fold(f.rsplit("/", 1)[-1][:-3]), []).append(f)
    findings = set()

    def add(check, path, flag=None):
        findings.add(("FAIL" if flag is None or flags[flag] else "WARN", check, path))

    if not found:
        add(1, settings["router_file"], "fail_on_missing_router_path")
    for r in rows:
        for p in r["paths"]:
            if not os.path.lexists(os.path.join(brain.home, p)):
                add(1, p, "fail_on_missing_router_path")
        row_channel = [brain.by_fold.get(fold(c)) for c in r["ch"]]
        row_channel = row_channel[0] if len(row_channel) == 1 else None
        for p in r["paths"]:
            if row_channel is None or brain.folder_channel(_relnorm(p)) != row_channel:
                add(6, p)
    for f in notes:
        info = brain.channel_info(f)
        tags = info["tags"] or set()
        chans = info["explicit"] | tags
        if not info["line"] and not info["labelled"] and not tags:
            add(2, f, "fail_on_untagged")
        if len(chans) > 1:
            add(3, f, "fail_on_multiple_channels")
        if len(chans) == 1 and brain.folder_channel(f) not in chans:
            add(4, f, "fail_on_folder_mismatch")
        if info["unknown"]:
            add(9, f)
        data = _read_text_file(os.path.join(brain.home, f))
        if data is None:
            continue
        text = data.decode("utf-8", "ignore")
        src_dir = f.rsplit("/", 1)[0]
        for target in link_targets(brain, f, text):
            linked = resolve_link(target, src_dir, note_set, stems)
            if linked is None or linked == f:
                continue
            other = brain.doctor_channels(linked)
            if chans and other and not other <= chans:
                add(5, f, "fail_on_cross_channel_link")
        if any(personal_data_hint(line) for line in text.splitlines()):
            findings.add(("WARN", 8, f))
    covered = [_relnorm(p) for r in rows for p in r["paths"]]
    for folder in sorted(set(f.rsplit("/", 1)[0] for f in notes)):
        if not _under(folder, covered):
            findings.add(("WARN", 7, folder + "/"))
    ordered = sorted(findings, key=lambda x: (x[1], x[2], x[0]))
    fails = [x for x in ordered if x[0] == "FAIL"]
    lines = ["%s %d %s" % (level, check, clean(path)) for level, check, path in ordered]
    lines.append("sb doctor: %d notes, %d router rows, %d failures, %d warnings" % (
        len(notes), len(rows), len(fails), len(ordered) - len(fails)))
    out.write("\n".join(lines) + "\n")
    if any(check != 1 for _, check, _ in fails):
        return 3
    return 1 if fails else 0


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- command line

def usage(settings):
    return "\n".join([
        "sb: fast, channel-aware search over your second brain (read-only).",
        "",
        "usage: sb <query...> [--channel %s] [--limit N] [--raw]" % "|".join(settings["channels"]),
        "                     [--engine auto|rg|python] [--config PATH]",
        "       sb --doctor [--config PATH]   # health check of the notes and the router",
        "       sb --init-key                 # create the scan key for name_hashes, once",
        "       sb --hash-name < words.txt    # the name_hashes key of each word (one per line)",
        "       sb --help",
        "",
        "Ranks router rows first (at most 3), then file hits: path:line, the best",
        "matching line and the note's channel (\"?\" = none). --channel X is strict:",
        "only notes of exactly channel X; untagged and mixed notes are withheld",
        "(the count is printed). Never reads dot files, *.env, *secret*, *token* or",
        "*credential* files and withholds lines that look like credentials. Raw",
        "notes only with --raw. --engine: auto (rg if installed, else python), rg",
        "or python; $SB_ENGINE sets the default.",
        "",
        "config: %s" % (settings["config_path"] or "none (built-in defaults)"),
        "home:   %s" % settings["home"],
        "",
    ])


def parse_argv(argv):
    opts = {"want": None, "limit": DEFAULT_LIMIT, "raw": False, "doctor": False, "help": False,
            "engine": None, "config": None, "query": [], "key_command": None, "flags": set()}
    it = iter(argv)

    def value(flag, inline):
        if inline is not None:
            return inline
        v = next(it, None)
        if v is None:
            raise UsageError("sb: %s needs a value" % flag)
        return v

    only_query = False
    for a in it:
        if only_query or not a.startswith("-") or a == "-":
            opts["query"].append(a)
            continue
        if a == "--":
            only_query = True
            continue
        flag, eq, inline = a.partition("=")
        inline = inline if eq else None
        opts["flags"].add(flag)
        if flag in ("-c", "--channel"):
            opts["want"] = next(it, "") if inline is None else inline
        elif flag in ("-n", "--limit"):
            v = value(flag, inline)
            if not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9]+", v) or int(v) < 1:
                raise UsageError("sb: --limit must be a whole number of at least 1")
            opts["limit"] = int(v)
        elif flag == "--engine":
            opts["engine"] = value(flag, inline)
        elif flag == "--config":
            opts["config"] = value(flag, inline)
        elif a == "--raw":
            opts["raw"] = True
        elif a == "--doctor":
            opts["doctor"] = True
        elif a in ("-h", "--help"):
            opts["help"] = True
        elif a in ("--init-key", "--hash-name"):
            opts["key_command"] = a
        else:
            raise UsageError("sb: unknown option (see sb --help)")
    if opts["key_command"] and (opts["query"] or opts["flags"] - {opts["key_command"], "--config"}):
        raise UsageError("sb: %s takes no other arguments" % opts["key_command"])
    return opts


def key_command(command, environ, out):
    """--init-key or --hash-name (words on stdin); neither reads the config."""
    if command == "--init-key":
        path = init_scan_key(environ)
        out.write("sb: created the scan key %s (%d random bytes, mode 0600, never printed); keep it out of "
                  "every repo and backup\n" % (path, KEY_BYTES))
        return 0
    key = read_scan_key(environ)
    try:
        text = sys.stdin.buffer.read().decode("utf-8")
    except UnicodeDecodeError:
        raise UsageError("sb: --hash-name reads UTF-8 text on stdin")
    hashes = hash_names(key, text)
    if hashes:
        out.write("\n".join(hashes) + "\n")
    return 0


def main(argv=None, environ=None):
    argv = sys.argv[1:] if argv is None else argv
    environ = os.environ if environ is None else environ
    out = sys.stdout
    try:
        opts = parse_argv(argv)
        if opts["key_command"]:
            return key_command(opts["key_command"], environ, out)
        settings = load_settings(opts["config"], environ)
    except UsageError as exc:
        print(str(exc), file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    except ConfigError as exc:
        print("sb: config error: %s" % exc, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    except ScanKeyError as exc:
        print("sb: %s" % exc, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if opts["help"]:
        out.write(usage(settings))
        return 0
    if settings["name_hashes"]:
        try:
            settings["name_key"] = read_scan_key(environ)
        except ScanKeyError as exc:
            print("sb: %s" % exc, file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
    if opts["doctor"]:
        return doctor(settings, out)
    want = opts["want"]
    if want is not None and want not in settings["channels"]:
        print("sb: --channel must be one of: %s" % ", ".join(settings["channels"]), file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    query = " ".join(opts["query"])
    if not terms_of(query):
        print("sb: no query terms (see sb --help)", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    try:
        engine, rg = pick_engine(opts["engine"], environ)
        return search(settings, query, want, opts["limit"], opts["raw"], engine, rg, out)
    except (UsageError, EngineError) as exc:
        print(str(exc), file=sys.stderr)
        return 2


if __name__ == "__main__":
    if hasattr(sys.stdout, "reconfigure"):
        sys.stdout.reconfigure(errors="replace")
    try:
        sys.exit(main())
    except BrokenPipeError:
        pass
